<title>FRANCE: Vallourec sees 1997 profit rise.</title>
<headline>Vallourec sees 1997 profit rise.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>French steel company Vallourec said it expects net consolidated profit to further rise in 1997 from an estimated 195 million francs in 1996 and 85 million francs in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;Prospects for 1997 are favourable and allow for a further rise in consolidated results, excluding the positive impact of a planned joint-venture with Mannesmannrohren-Werke, which will impact results from 1998,&quot; Vallourec said in a statement.</p>
<p>Vallourec plans to merge its unwelded steel tubes business with that of Mannesmannrohren-Werke.</p>
<p>Vallourec also said it plans to raise 1996 net dividend to six francs per share fom five francs in 1995 .</p>
<p>The 1996 profit figure includes a net tax charge of 40 million francs, 19 million francs in goodwill amortisation and 289 million francs in fixed assets depreciation.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
